IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wc-maintenance-enforcement`

-- Women's Charter 1961, ss 71, 80, 81, 83, 91B, 91D, 91K, 91L, 91N, 91O, 91P, 91R -- worked cases for REQ-0269.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case, the Family Justice Rules or the Women's Charter (Maintenance Enforcement) regulations (none was retrieved).
-- Expected results were written by hand from the text.

-- REQ-0269 (Jun Hao scenario, event j071, 15 January 2039): a father ordered to pay $600 a month for his child misses three
-- payments ($1,800). His ex-partner, who applied for the order, applies to enforce it. He is employed. Nothing is paid by
-- the hearing.
`the Jun Hao default` MEANS EnforcementCase WITH
    `the court is satisfied the order was breached` IS TRUE
    `a consent order was made` IS FALSE
    `arrears owing when the application was made` IS 1800
    `arrears still unpaid` IS 1800
    `a show-payment order was made on an earlier date in this application` IS FALSE
    `counselling is in the interests of the parties or their children` IS TRUE
    `suitable community service arrangements can be made` IS TRUE
    `the respondent has an employer or pension payer` IS TRUE

-- The same default, but he pays the $1,800 after the application and before the hearing.
`arrears paid up before the hearing` MEANS EnforcementCase WITH
    `the court is satisfied the order was breached` IS TRUE
    `a consent order was made` IS FALSE
    `arrears owing when the application was made` IS 1800
    `arrears still unpaid` IS 0
    `a show-payment order was made on an earlier date in this application` IS FALSE
    `counselling is in the interests of the parties or their children` IS TRUE
    `suitable community service arrangements can be made` IS TRUE
    `the respondent has an employer or pension payer` IS TRUE

-- The parties agree terms and the court makes a consent order; he is unemployed.
`a consent order with an unemployed father` MEANS EnforcementCase WITH
    `the court is satisfied the order was breached` IS FALSE
    `a consent order was made` IS TRUE
    `arrears owing when the application was made` IS 1800
    `arrears still unpaid` IS 1800
    `a show-payment order was made on an earlier date in this application` IS FALSE
    `counselling is in the interests of the parties or their children` IS FALSE
    `suitable community service arrangements can be made` IS FALSE
    `the respondent has an employer or pension payer` IS FALSE

-- The court is not satisfied of any breach (he proves he paid).
`no breach shown` MEANS EnforcementCase WITH
    `the court is satisfied the order was breached` IS FALSE
    `a consent order was made` IS FALSE
    `arrears owing when the application was made` IS 0
    `arrears still unpaid` IS 0
    `a show-payment order was made on an earlier date in this application` IS FALSE
    `counselling is in the interests of the parties or their children` IS FALSE
    `suitable community service arrangements can be made` IS FALSE
    `the respondent has an employer or pension payer` IS TRUE

-- A show-payment order was made at an earlier hearing on this same application.
`after a show-payment order` MEANS EnforcementCase WITH
    `the court is satisfied the order was breached` IS TRUE
    `a consent order was made` IS FALSE
    `arrears owing when the application was made` IS 1800
    `arrears still unpaid` IS 1800
    `a show-payment order was made on an earlier date in this application` IS TRUE
    `counselling is in the interests of the parties or their children` IS TRUE
    `suitable community service arrangements can be made` IS TRUE
    `the respondent has an employer or pension payer` IS TRUE

-- REQ-0269 FIRST: the requirement's own question on its facts.
-- The court must declare the $1,800, order it paid and proved, and specify a default term (s 81(2)) ...
#ASSERT `the court must declare the arrears and order them paid and proved` `the Jun Hao default` FALSE
#ASSERT `the court must specify a default term of imprisonment` `the Jun Hao default` FALSE FALSE
-- ... and YES, it may attach his wages (s 91B(1)(g)) ...
#ASSERT `the court may make the enforcement order` `an attachment of earnings order` `the Jun Hao default`
-- ... and all seven s 91B orders are open on these facts ...
#ASSERT `the number of enforcement orders open` `the Jun Hao default` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the court may make the enforcement order` `imprisonment for the arrears` `the Jun Hao default`
#ASSERT `the court may make the enforcement order` `a warrant to levy the arrears as for a fine` `the Jun Hao default`
#ASSERT `the court may make the enforcement order` `attachment of a debt` `the Jun Hao default`
-- ... imprisonment of up to 3 months (one per month's worth, s 91P(1)(a)); a guarantee of up to $1,800 (s 91L(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment for arrears in months` 1800 600 FALSE EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the largest banker's guarantee` 600 EQUALS 1800
-- She may apply, and once the arrears are declared she may report them to the credit bureau (s 83); they are 3 months old,
-- well within s 91R(4).
#ASSERT `may apply to enforce the maintenance order` `the person who applied for the maintenance order` FALSE
#ASSERT `may lodge an arrears report with the credit bureau` `the payee or the beneficiary` TRUE 1800
#ASSERT `the arrears are recoverable` 3 FALSE FALSE

-- s 80: who may apply.
#ASSERT `may apply to enforce the maintenance order` `a payee with custody or care and control of the child` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `may apply to enforce the maintenance order` `anyone else` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `may apply to enforce the maintenance order` `a payee who is a trustee of the child` TRUE

-- s 81(1)(a), (4)(b), 91B, 91P(3)(a), (4), 91N(2): which orders are open.
#ASSERT `the number of enforcement orders open` `no breach shown` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make the enforcement order` `imprisonment for the arrears` `a consent order with an unemployed father`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make the enforcement order` `an attachment of earnings order` `a consent order with an unemployed father`
#ASSERT `the court may make the enforcement order` `a banker's guarantee against future default` `a consent order with an unemployed father`
-- warrant, attachment of a debt and the guarantee: 3 of 7.
#ASSERT `the number of enforcement orders open` `a consent order with an unemployed father` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the court may make the enforcement order` `imprisonment for the arrears` `arrears paid up before the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make the enforcement order` `a warrant to levy the arrears as for a fine` `arrears paid up before the hearing`
-- imprisonment, guarantee, counselling, community service, attachment of earnings: 5 of 7.
#ASSERT `the number of enforcement orders open` `arrears paid up before the hearing` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make the enforcement order` `imprisonment for the arrears` `after a show-payment order`

-- s 81(2), (7): dismissed applications and special circumstances.
#ASSERT NOT `the court must declare the arrears and order them paid and proved` `the Jun Hao default` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the court must specify a default term of imprisonment` `the Jun Hao default` FALSE TRUE

-- s 91P(1): the cap. $1,900 is 3 months' worth and a part: 4. The Illustration's $5,000 on $1,000: 5. Lump sum: 6.
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment for arrears in months` 1900 600 FALSE EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment for arrears in months` 5000 1000 FALSE EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment for arrears in months` 1800 600 TRUE EQUALS 6

-- s 81(5): the default term. One failure on arrears (6) plus $600 of payable maintenance unproved (1) = 7.
#ASSERT `the maximum default term in months` 1 600 600 EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the maximum default term in months` 0 1000 600 EQUALS 2

-- s 91O(1): no imprisonment where good cause is shown.
#ASSERT NOT `the court may imprison for breaching the show-payment order` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the court may imprison for breaching the show-payment order` TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- ss 91L, 91N: guarantee period and community service hours.
#ASSERT `the longest banker's guarantee in months` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `the most community service hours` EQUALS 40

-- s 71(3): no separate s 71 application while Part 9 proceedings are pending.
#ASSERT NOT `a section 71 attachment of earnings application may be made` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `a section 71 attachment of earnings application may be made` TRUE FALSE

-- s 91D(2): the employer need not comply until 7 days after service. s 91K: $2,000 and 12 months.
#ASSERT `the employer must already comply` 8
#ASSERT `the maximum fine for disobeying an attachment of earnings order` EQUALS 2000

-- s 83: the credit bureau report needs a declaration and an amount still owing.
#ASSERT NOT `may lodge an arrears report with the credit bureau` `the payee or the beneficiary` FALSE 1800
#ASSERT NOT `may lodge an arrears report with the credit bureau` `someone other than these` TRUE 1800

-- s 91R(4): arrears more than 3 years old are barred unless earlier proceedings or special circumstances.
#ASSERT NOT `the arrears are recoverable` 37 FALSE FALSE
